        "text": "If you need to change the text color on mouseover for all elements of a certain type, then using CSS is the best option.",
        "type": "text"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 2: JavaScript `addEventListener` (More Control)\n\nThis approach gives you more flexibility, especially for dynamic behavior.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <body>\n    <span id=\"mySpan\">Hover over me!</span>\n\n    <script>\n      const span = document.getElementById('mySpan');\n\n      span.addEventListener('mouseover', function () {\n        span.style.color = 'red';\n      });\n\n      span.addEventListener('mouseout', function () {\n        span.style.color = 'black'; // Revert color on mouse out\n      });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\n",
