  "answer_text": "There are **three ways** to change a `<span>`'s color on mouse over:\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 1: CSS `:hover` (Recommended)\n\nThis is the simplest and cleanest approach.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <style>\n      span:hover {\n        color: red;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <span>Hover over me!</span>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\nIf you need to change the text color on mouseover for all elements of a certain type, then using CSS is the best option.\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 2: JavaScript `addEventListener` (More Control)\n\nThis approach gives you more flexibility, especially for dynamic behavior.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <body>\n    <span id=\"mySpan\">Hover over me!</span>\n\n    <script>\n      const span = document.getElementById('mySpan');\n\n      span.addEventListener('mouseover', function () {\n        span.style.color = 'red';\n      });\n\n      span.addEventListener('mouseout', function () {\n        span.style.color = 'black'; // Revert color on mouse out\n      });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\nAdd a `mouseover` event to the element, changing its text color when the user hovers over it, and add a `mouseout` event to the element, changing its text color back to the default when the user moves their cursor out.\n\nIf you need to change the text color on mouseover for a specific element, or if you need to change the text color dynamically, then using JavaScript is the best option.\n\n---\n\n## \u2705 Method 3: Inline `onmouseover` Attribute\n\nA quick and simple inline approach directly in the HTML tag.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <body>\n    <span\n      onmouseover=\"this.style.color='red'\"\n      onmouseout=\"this.style.color='black'\"\n    >\n      Hover over me!\n    </span>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\nThe `onmouseover` event is triggered when the user hovers over an element with the mouse.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfc6 Which method should you use?\n\n| Method | Best For |\n|---|---|\n| **CSS `:hover`** | Simple, static color changes \u2014 cleanest code |\n| **JS `addEventListener`** | Dynamic or programmatic color changes |\n| **Inline `onmouseover`** | Quick prototypes, but not recommended for large projects |\n\nFor most use cases, the **CSS `:hover`** method is preferred as it keeps styling separate from logic and requires the least code.",
